kirby kirby kirby that's a name you  should know kirby kirby kirby he's the  star of the show he's more than you  think he's got maximum pink  kirby  that's right kirby the super tough pink  puff himself is back for an all-new 3d  adventure game and with the release date  right around the corner here's  everything to know about kirby in the  forgotten land  [Music]  kirby in the forgotten land begins with  kirby and his warp star getting sucked  into a rift in the sky transporting him  to  you guessed it a forgotten land that is  also pretty mysterious with what looks  to be abandoned structures from a past  civilization  kinda like horizon zero dawn you think  kirby will get his own focus  [Music]  anyways kirby discovers the ruins of  waddle dee town and learns that the  waddle dees are being kidnapped by the  beast pack a new group of villains  you'll be fighting in this game with  enemies as adorable as this fox-like  creature named  i love that name an enemy is as strong  and evil as the strong r b scory mondo  and the lethal leopard claraline to stop  these evildoers and rescue the waddle  dees kirby partners up with alphalin  this turquoise thing with giant ears and  sets off to suck up things and steal  abilities like kirby always does good  thing kirby is constantly put in  situations where sucking up enemies is a  useful ability otherwise he would be  screwed  kirby in the forgotten land is a 3d  platforming adventure game developed by  hal laboratory the company that's been  making kirby games since the very  beginning it's not an open world game  however it's still split up into linear  levels like previous platforming kirby  adventures each stage is a 3d  environment with hidden wattle d's to  discover and optional hidden objectives  and some of these stages include boss  fights like the two characters i  mentioned before you'll also collect  capsule toys and star coins capsule toys  are just fun collectibles and star coins  can be used in wattle d-town but more on  that later to get from level to level  there is an overworld map where you can  use the warp star to fly around and on  top of main levels there are also  treasure road levels a sort of race to  the finish style minigame where you're  given a specific copy ability or  mouthful mode and have to try and beat  the level as fast as possible each level  has a target time as well that rewards  you with more star coins if you hit it  beating these levels mainly rewards you  with rare stones which you can also use  in waddle d-town but again  more on that later one of the brand new  features in forgotten land is mouthful  mode where you can suck up objects and  take advantage of their abilities some  of the mouthful mode abilities we know  about are carmouth which turns kirby  into a car for faster traversal and to  ram into enemies vending mouth which  turns kirby into a vending machine and  gives kirby the ability to shoot cans at  enemies cone mouth which lets kirby slam  into objects using the pointy side of  the cone scissor lift mouth which gives  kirby a way to reach high places ring  mouth which unlike the doorbell shoots  out gusts of wind which can help push  boats across water or spin fans light  bulb mouth which can illuminate dark  areas arc mouth which turns kirby into a  paraglider and allows him to fly and  there's even water balloon mouth which  fills up kirby with water that can be  used to spray enemies or clean up goo  anyways that's a lot and there are  probably a whole lot more throughout the  game but i've already said a mouthful  so let's move on on top of mouthful mode  there's also the copy abilities we know  and love kirby for like sword bomb  tornado and fire however in forgotten  land you can now evolve copy abilities  for example fire can become volcano fire  and volcano fire could become dragon  fire where you can like get dragon wings  and fly around like shoot a flamethrower  out of your mouth looks pretty awesome  there's also and i'm just going to list  them off now chalk room cutter clutter  needle  gigant sword noble ranger frosty ice toy  hammer and probably so much more that  we've only seen mere glimpses of there  are also brand new copy abilities like  the drill that lets you go underground  before attacking and ranger which lets  you fire star bullets at your foes pew  pew  you can evolve your copy abilities at  the weapon shop in waddle d-town by  finding hidden blueprints throughout the  levels remember those star coins and  rare stones i mentioned earlier the  weapon shop in waddle d-town is one of  the places to use them as they're  essentially the currency needed to  evolve copy abilities after finding the  blueprints waddle d-town itself is a hub  world that grows and expands the more  waddle dees you save throughout the game  there's plenty of other things to do in  waddle d-town too like shopping  eating working at a restaurant fishing  collecting capsule toys and even  watching cutscenes again at a little  waddle d theater there's also a coliseum  you can unlock in wild with the town  where you can fight a bunch of enemies  including returning character meta  knight speaking of waddle dees and  waddle d-town the game also includes a  two-player co-op mode where the second  player can play as bandana waddle d this  ability is available very early on in  the game after the intro level so like  many other switch games you can share  the joy and pass a joy con to a friend  there are also two difficulty modes  spring breeze mode and wild mode spring  breeze mode claims to be simple to play  with a lot of health for the adventure  and the perfect mode for those new to  action games while wild mode claims to  be a bit more challenging while also  giving you more star coins as rewards  the difficulty options can be changed at  any time so feel free to try both  kirby and the forgotten land will be  exclusive to nintendo's switch and will  work on all nintendo switch models  whether you have the original the switch  light or the oled model or oled model  however you want to call it but unless  you have a separate pair of joy-cons you  won't be able to take advantage of the  two-player co-op on the switch light  since the controllers are attached to  that system so keep that in mind  kirby in the forgotten land doesn't have  any planned dlc at the moment but i'm  going to take this opportunity to talk  about the game's amiibo support because  that's kind of the physical equivalent  of dlc right anyways there aren't any  new kirby amiibo being released  alongside forgotten land but all the  curvy amiibo throughout the years are  compatible with the game including the  smash bros and kirby versions of kirby  meta knight and king dedede as well as  the waddle d amiibo and the qb amiibo  non-kirby series amiibo are also  compatible these are just the ones  highlighted by nintendo what do these  amiibo do exactly tapping non-kirby  amiibo gives you recovery items and star  coins and tapping any of the amiibo  listed above gives you even better  recovery items and even better star  coins so ultimately it's a nice bonus  for those who want it  kirby in the forgotten land launches on  march 25th 2022 for 59.99 and it'll be  available physically in stores as well  as on the nintendo eshop there is a demo  available to download right now for free  on the nintendo eshop that includes  three stages in the first world if  you're looking to try the game for  yourself before buying completing the  demo and finding all the hidden waddle  dees also gives you two present codes  that can be used in the final release at  waddle deliveries in waddle dee town  it's another cute name i really like  that name waddle dee liveries  waddle these nuts  right now there's no collector's edition  or special edition or ultra epic super  mega deluxe edition for the game however  in the u.s if you pre-order the game  from walmart you'll receive a popsocket  of kirby and if you pre-order the game  from gamestop you'll get a pin set if  you're in the uk and pre-order from the  my nintendo store you'll receive a free  notebook and magnet sheet and if you  pre-order from amazon uk you'll just get  the magnet sheet no other retailer has  announced a pre-order bonus at the time  of making this video or i missed  something and you can all yell at me in  the comments about it lucky for us more  comments means more engagement so i dare  you to do it and there you have it  everything to know about kirby and the  forgotten land thank you so much for  watching and for more on kirby in the  forgotten land you can check out the  written preview by stephen petit on our  website gamespot.com as well as 10  minutes of gameplay from the full retail  release here on our youtube channel with  a review coming soon oh and it's also  kirby's 30th anniversary this year happy  30th kirby
 

